1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,697
BRAMBLE: Case open!

2
00:00:01,697 --> 00:00:05,327
IVY: Hey! That's not fair! Otto got more!

3
00:00:05,527 --> 00:00:08,982
OTTO: I counted eleven acorns. You have ten!

4
00:00:09,382 --> 00:00:14,250
Today's case: counting to ten, one acorn at a time.

5
00:00:14,550 --> 00:00:17,219
It's like a sausage sizzle.

6
00:00:17,419 --> 00:00:20,747
One sausage goes on each bread.

7
00:00:20,947 --> 00:00:24,421
One number goes with each thing.

8
00:00:25,021 --> 00:00:31,301
OTTO: One, two, three, four, five, six.

9
00:00:31,201 --> 00:00:35,679
OTTO: Seven, eight, nine, ten, eleven!

10
00:00:36,079 --> 00:00:38,223
IVY: Hmm. Something looks funny.

11
00:00:38,623 --> 00:00:41,225
BRAMBLE: Let's not guess. Let's test.

12
00:00:41,625 --> 00:00:44,662
BRAMBLE: Can you point to each acorn?

13
00:00:48,262 --> 00:00:50,453
BRAMBLE: Who has more acorns?

14
00:00:50,853 --> 00:00:53,294
A. Otto has more.

15
00:00:53,494 --> 00:00:56,084
B. They have the same.

16
00:00:56,284 --> 00:00:58,197
Pause and think.

17
00:01:02,797 --> 00:01:05,969
A ten frame has ten boxes.

18
00:01:06,169 --> 00:01:10,194
Move each acorn once. Say one number.

19
00:01:10,594 --> 00:01:14,914
One, two, three, four, five.

20
00:01:15,114 --> 00:01:19,110
Six, seven, eight, nine, ten.

21
00:01:19,510 --> 00:01:23,035
The last number tells how many. Ten!

22
00:01:23,835 --> 00:01:26,784
OTTO: Oh! I counted one acorn twice!

23
00:01:27,184 --> 00:01:29,806
Both have ten. It's B!

24
00:01:30,206 --> 00:01:34,151
BRAMBLE: Let's check another way. Make pairs.

25
00:01:34,551 --> 00:01:37,248
Every acorn has a partner.

26
00:01:37,648 --> 00:01:40,223
IVY: Ten and ten. The same!

27
00:01:40,623 --> 00:01:42,119
BRAMBLE: Case solved!

28
00:01:43,619 --> 00:01:46,502
OTTO: Now let's count your spines, Bramble!

29
00:01:46,702 --> 00:01:49,349
BRAMBLE: I have about five thousand.

30
00:01:49,549 --> 00:01:52,589
OTTO: One, two, three... maybe tomorrow!

31
00:01:53,189 --> 00:01:58,274
Say it with me. The last number tells how many.

32
00:02:00,074 --> 00:02:04,911
Try it at home. Count ten pegs into a cup.

33
00:02:05,411 --> 00:02:08,730
Next case: a missing house number.

